u(10,164,212,'Scene startup',[41,73,94,153],'initialized board/rules → UI → later admission guard','Scene receives the battle object, creates viewport at99999 and asks for TripleTriad background and a bottom64-high help window.','Nine tile sprites follow board order with78 horizontal/94 vertical spacing; tile elemental backs use the same board type.','Creates five player placeholders, original-index tables, hand/board image tables, name and score layers.','Opponent label is left and player label right; text is read from supplied battle name fields.','Requests Triple Triad music and a fade-in while updating sprites; startup precedes the insufficient-card return.',disposition='PRESENTATION_REQUEST_AND_CONTROL_ORDER_RECORDED')
u(11,214,220,'Scene normal shutdown',[77,84,115,153],'normal duel/early guard → music fade → UI disposal','Requests a1.0-second BGM fade, then sprite fade-out, sprite-hash disposal, tile bitmap disposal and viewport disposal in that order.','No local ensure promises complete scene cleanup on exceptions; explicit normal early returns call this shutdown.')
u(12,222,231,'Timed notification',[108,111],'text assignment → uptime/update loop → next duel phase','The1.5-second timer starts when text is assigned.','Every loop updates graphics/input/sprites before checking elapsed time; USE and BACK cannot shorten this wait.','This is an uptime threshold observed after updates, not a frame-count or full-text-completion condition.')
u(13,233,251,'Paused confirmation',[94,109,111],'result text → USE wait → persistent transfer','Enables letter-by-letter and appends a pause marker.','USE on busy text resumes it, with decision sound only at an actual pause; USE when no longer busy exits.','BACK is not handled by this local confirmation loop.','Normal exit disables letter-by-letter and clears the help text; result storage transfer occurs after this return.')
u(14,253,256,'Notification hand snapshots',[73,115],'cloned caller hands → original display identity arrays','Scene stores supplied player/opponent arrays.','Real caller passes independent shallow clones of symbol identity arrays, so later hand deletion preserves the scene original-index lookup.')
u(15,258,346,'Manual hand preparation',[61,63,104],'persistent slots → prepared copy → manual hand','Commands preserve prepared-copy order and display species name with per-slot quantity; highlight requests preview.','Every cycle updates command navigation and preview before local BACK>USE trigger arbitration.','BACK restores the last chosen identity to the temporary copy; with zero choices it only buzzes, suppressing same-cycle USE.','USE selects only a nonempty slot, appends its identity and removes one from the temporary copy.','Five choices hide/deactivate command and preview; a later USE confirms the complete hand; BACK can still undo.','Selected images show only chosen count; final disposal closes temporary selection widgets.','Permanent card warehouse is never debited during this preparation.')
u(16,348,357,'Player hand display',[61,73],'random hand → face sprites → scene identity lookup','Random-hand path creates five face images in hand order and stores their images.','Original indexes keep per-card identity stable when remaining-hand arrays later shrink.',disposition='PRESENTATION_REQUEST_AND_CONTROL_ORDER_RECORDED')
u(17,359,369,'Opponent hand display',[50,73,86],'opponent original hand → open/closed sprites','Five opponent slots show faces only under openhand; otherwise they show backs.','Original opponent indexes are saved for later placement/highlight compaction.',disposition='PRESENTATION_REQUEST_AND_CONTROL_ORDER_RECORDED')
u(18,371,405,'View opponent remaining hand',[80,86,106],'player hand count argument + opponent index list → highlight','Initial highlight is0; DOWN>UP>BACK is the mutually exclusive action chain.','Navigation wraps using the supplied player numCards argument, while rendering iterates only opponent remaining indexes.','For player5/opponent4, UP from0 reaches position4 with no highlighted visible card; DOWN returns0.','BACK sets−1, redraws all surviving opponent cards unselected, then returns; USE alone does not exit.','No card, hand count or board state is modified.')
u(19,407,450,'Choose player card',[79,80,86,105],'remaining player hand → selected index or opponent inspection','Starts focus0 and displays the openhand-dependent prompt.','Mutually exclusive priority is DOWN repeat, UP repeat, USE trigger, ACTION trigger when openhand.','UP/DOWN wrap by current player count; USE accepts selected index.','After opponent inspection returns, prompt/focus reset to0; source text naming Z does not identify a physical key.')
u(20,452,510,'Choose board position',[81,82,107],'selected hand index → position/nil → caller commit','Starts at top-left; preview is moved above board while other hand sprites compact.','Mutually exclusive priority DOWN>UP>LEFT>RIGHT>BACK>USE uses repeat for directions and trigger for buttons.','Each axis cursor wraps across board dimensions independent of wrap capture rule.','BACK returns nil before any board/card/hand write.','USE on occupied square buzzes and stays; USE on empty square accepts coordinate and lowers sprite layer.')
u(21,512,520,'Finish player placement visuals',[73,84,94],'caller board commit/flip + original identity snapshot → board image','Moves chosen original sprite into board-index table and recreates card from scene original hand identity.','Refreshes board ownership visuals, deletes chosen remaining sprite index, then updates score.','It follows real model hand deletion; snapshot and shrinking current indexes preserve selected identity.')
u(22,522,540,'Opponent move presentation',[83,84],'AI selected identity/position → opponent reveal/move request','Replaces selected remaining opponent sprite image with a face, disposing its previous image.','Moves selected card to board coordinate, compacts other remaining sprites without committing model ownership itself.')
u(23,542,550,'Finish opponent placement visuals',[73,84,94],'caller board commit/flip → scene refresh','Stores selected original opponent sprite/card at board index.','Refreshes colors, deletes that remaining opponent index, then recomputes displayed score.')
